# CQ 08: Where do the kind of action and the kind of path differ?
#
# The case the standard warns about. Entry 351-47-06 defines the reset circuit
# as a switching system with a closed action path containing at least one
# binary storage element, and its note states that it has an open action
# despite the closed path.
#
# A model reading a closed path as a closed loop would type it wrongly, and
# test case 3 is built to be exactly that trap. The three kinds are reported
# side by side so the divergence is visible rather than inferred: the path is
# closed, the action is open, and the control is an open-loop control.
#
# Cases 1 and 2 agree in all three and answer empty. That the question returns
# nothing there is what makes the one row of case 3 mean something.
PREFIX iec60050:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iec60050#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?control ?controlKind ?actionKind ?pathKind
WHERE {
  ?control iec60050:runsOverActionPath ?path ; iec60050:hasAction ?action .
  ?path   a ?pathKind   . FILTER(?pathKind   IN (iec60050:OpenActionPath, iec60050:ClosedActionPath))
  ?action a ?actionKind . FILTER(?actionKind IN (iec60050:OpenAction,     iec60050:ClosedAction))
  ?control a ?controlKind .
  FILTER(?controlKind IN (iec60050:OpenLoopControl, iec60050:ClosedLoopControl))
  FILTER(
    (?pathKind = iec60050:ClosedActionPath && ?actionKind = iec60050:OpenAction) ||
    (?pathKind = iec60050:OpenActionPath   && ?actionKind = iec60050:ClosedAction) ||
    (?actionKind = iec60050:ClosedAction   && ?controlKind = iec60050:OpenLoopControl) ||
    (?actionKind = iec60050:OpenAction     && ?controlKind = iec60050:ClosedLoopControl)
  )
} ORDER BY ?control
